  :seon.task/plan "What is wrong: root's walk of an agent's branch (seon.render.proc/branch-walk!, and its cold draws) reads seon.render/declared-var under root's registry, not the branch's: seon.render.proc binds none, so a layout the agent registered on its branch draws on its own walk (seon.repl/the-walk, what its model reads) and not on the page root serves for an ended agent. Found by the sweep of step 2 of the finished task one-way-to-make-what-an-agent-is-sent, whose fix for a walk's held layout has no reach here. What should be true: docs/ctx.md's page is the agent's to change holds for every reader of its page, live or ended; seon.repl/branch-registry reads a branch's schema changes, and the same read serves root's walk. Proof: an ended agent's page, drawn by root, shows the layout its branch registered."
